<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak stats bureau details 1996 real GDP growth. [CORRECTED 13:15 GMT]</title>
<headline>Slovak stats bureau details 1996 real GDP growth. [CORRECTED 13:15 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are details of full year 1996 gross domestic product (GDP) as released by the Slovak Statistical Bureau (SUSR) on Wednesday:</p>
<p> GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT	     1996    Jan-Sep'96   1995</p>
<p>  real change yr/yr (pct)	   +6.8	+7.0	 +6.8</p>
<p>(Corrects real GDP growth for 1996 from +6.9 to +6.8 percent)</p>
<p>  absolute amount (SKK bln)	443.3     432.7	414.5</p>
<p>(pct change)</p>
<p>  household demand		    +7.2	+7.8	 +3.4</p>
<p>  state administration demand    +24.2     +25.2	 +1.6</p>
<p>  gross capital creation	   +33.3     +30.5	 +5.8</p>
<p>  exports of goods/services	 -1.6	-3.9	 +3.5</p>
<p>  imports of goods/services	+18.5     +15.4	 +9.6</p>
<p>change in stocks and reserves</p>
<p>   (SKK bln)			    +6.5	 n/a	 -3.5</p>
<p>Note. SUSR released the real year-on-year change figure on Tuesday, but did not give any details at the time.</p>
<p>All figures are preliminary and subjects to revision. Earlier this month SUSR said it had revised the 1995 GDP growth figure to 6.8 percent year-on-year from the previously reported 7.4 percent growth.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
